We are updating an existing plugin that provides the option of having confirmation messages appear to users in a popup modal after a successful Gravity Forms form submission. Currently, site administrators have to add a CSS class to the form in order to have the popup modal display to their users after a successful form submittion. In this update, we're going to add options to the confirmation interface to allow administrators to have the message displayed in a popup modal without the need to add the CSS class to the form.

Tasks
- Add option to the admin page for Gravity Form form confirmations with a group label of "Popup Confirmation" and a checkbox with a label of "Display this message as a popup/modal."
- Add conditional display of new option to only display when text (message) is selected as the confirmation type.
- When the confirmation settings are saved, the value of the new checkbox needs to be saved to form object using GFAPI. The value should be added to the confirmations object of the form, within the confirmation being saved, with a key of "displayModal."
- Upon load/reload, the checkbox value should indicate the value of displayModal for the confirmation being edited.
- If displayModal is true, the message of the confirmation should be displayed in a popup modal.

Backwards Compatibility
- Keep all existing functionality that checks for the CSS class gf_confirmation_popup to display confirmation messages in a popup modal.

Design
- Keep all existing design.

Assessibility
- Check for any assessibility issues and recommend improvements.

Security
- Check for any security issues and recommend improvements.
